.TH tuawk n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuawk
.PP
An awk\-style record/field processor in pure Tcl. Records map to fields, rules are \fB{pattern action}\fR pairs, with \fBBEGIN\fR/\fBEND\fR. It is not an awk\-language interpreter: patterns are Tcl expressions (or \fB/regex/\fR against \fB$0\fR) and actions are Tcl scripts.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tuawk 0.2
.CE
.SS API
.IP \(bu
\fBtuawk::run text rules ?\-fs SEP? ?\-ofs SEP? ?\-ors SEP?\fR \-> collected output
.IP \(bu
\fBtuawk::file path rules ...\fR                            \-> over a file
.PP
\fBrules\fR is a flat list of pattern/action pairs:
.IP \(bu
Pattern: empty matches always; \fB/regex/\fR matches \fB$0\fR; otherwise a Tcl \fBexpr\fR (e.g. \fB$3 > 100\fR, \fB$NF == 0\fR). Special \fBBEGIN\fR / \fBEND\fR run before/after records.
.IP \(bu
Action: a Tcl script. An empty action means \fBemit $0\fR.
.IP \(bu
Fields: \fB$0\fR (whole record), \fB$1\fR..\fB$NF\fR, \fB$NR\fR. \fBNR\fR and \fBNF\fR start at 0, so they are set in \fBBEGIN\fR and in \fBEND\fR even without any record.
.IP \(bu
Variables set in actions persist across records (like awk globals), ideal for aggregation with BEGIN/END. All rules of one call run in one private frame (a coroutine in a sandbox namespace that is deleted afterwards): \fBset x\fR always creates a rule variable and never touches a global \fBx\fR, under Tcl 8.6 and 9 alike. \fBvariable x\fR is not needed (but still works).
.IP \(bu
In an action, \fBbreak\fR skips the remaining rules for the current record (like awk \fBnext\fR); \fBcontinue\fR goes on with the next rule.
.IP \(bu
\fBemit args...\fR prints (joined by OFS, terminated by ORS).
.PP
Options: \fB\-fs\fR (default whitespace runs; one char = \fBsplit\fR; multiple = regex), \fB\-ofs\fR (default \fB" "\fR), \fB\-ors\fR (default \fB"\en"\fR).
.PP
Errors: unknown option or an option without value \fBTCLUTILS TUAWK OPTION\fR; an odd \fBrules\fR list \fBTCLUTILS TUAWK RULES\fR. Errors in patterns and actions pass through unchanged (a field beyond \fBNF\fR: \fBTCL LOOKUP VARNAME n\fR).
.CS
tuawk::run "a b c\nd e f" {{} {emit $2}}              ;# -> "b\ne\n"
tuawk::run $data {BEGIN {set s 0} {} {set s [expr {$s+$1}]} END {emit "sum: $s"}}
.CE
.SS CLI
.CS
tclsh bin/tuawk.tcl -fs : '{$3 >= 1000} {emit $1 $3}' /etc/passwd
cat log | tclsh bin/tuawk.tcl '/ERROR/ {emit $NR $0}'
.CE
.SS Scope
.PP
Records are lines; no custom record separator. A field access beyond \fBNF\fR is an error, not a silent empty value (intentional). For full awk programs use \fBexec awk\fR.
